\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 The trade-off, stated plainly\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 As-of resolution is slightly harder to query than a snapshot, and a careless join can return two rows for one skill if 
\f4\fs26 valid_from
\f0\fs24  and 
\f4\fs26 valid_to
\f0\fs24  ever overlap. The filtered unique index on open rows prevents the common version of that bug, and routing all reads through the view prevents the rest.\
In exchange you stop duplicating a dimension you don't own, you capture changes made by other teams, and you get a verifiable record of exactly what each model run was given. For an exercise whose whole purpose is to measure whether definition changes improved accuracy, that last point is worth the extra join.\
}